[{"id":"VRCE-2-64-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":1,"english":"Bharata was speaking thus when the envoys with their vehicles fatigued, entered the splendid royal residence surrounded by a strong rampart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7936f0b6431910b248df1d9208d3e22b8a604ac7efdf5b81b35e8a12d6ffbacb","compact":"bd629a8afe5343acc48271a0894d3c642ba68d4fca8523e4510ccc724d4a079c","nasal":"34a8810929f33a1c52cccb918767604ab71b69af508e7e0775d84fdd5210c8f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":2,"english":"Presenting themselves before the king, they, well received by him as well as the prince, bowed down to the feet of the monarch.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.597,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"096cacd05e7ab5dab6ae12574ef1eb93b4932195fd87f6d0c588dac9f570c728","compact":"b5267825fa91c7cf23cab3e1f9030dcd61976aa2e1a22d2301a16ff3c1d225eb","nasal":"b5267825fa91c7cf23cab3e1f9030dcd61976aa2e1a22d2301a16ff3c1d225eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":3,"english":"The priest as well as the counsellors have enquired after your welfare. Do you at once set out. A business is at hand that brooks no delay on your part.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.897,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-68-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aaeb372d73c100d4808a6f0cb57b02c6a2676d8121b9a11ca4bdcae3f33930d2","compact":"9d9f2e8e461b13b2bb9a41161304e8eb8652baabad257f387102d09d385fceac","nasal":"28cb2b1cfd8b0dc7a0c782d21def990fc39dabb59be512595889a24e3c39f5b7"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":4,"english":"Twenty Kotis are intended for the king and complete ten for your maternal uncle, O son of the monarch.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3418dff43074a6e9ddd8b2439145771b0d9cd017abd7333a050112fb376f9d0","compact":"4017f95c8cc647f996f8a3e0de2e3b01df7bc28a9c6e523f002011a25980d335","nasal":"4017f95c8cc647f996f8a3e0de2e3b01df7bc28a9c6e523f002011a25980d335"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":5,"english":"Taking all these, Bharata attached to his relatives, made the articles over to them; and receiving the envoys with goodly gifts, spoke to them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.631,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"10e4e9886f784fdcf0a06b00e5527ded38360b887aa7104c0075799bc958a71c","compact":"b42d685f45d464285cf897afc12bc5afb5a9ade8b1442e300568def46d78dd69","nasal":"b42d685f45d464285cf897afc12bc5afb5a9ade8b1442e300568def46d78dd69"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":6,"english":"Is my father, king Dasaratha, well? And is it well with Rama and the high-souled Laksmana?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.362,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2070e10537297732b1fe89642564fda2b90a4419856d7292810de92a46eb38ec","compact":"73fdf47094c36ad3452a267cefd9329c4374ecb04f0bfe1e8e68cd9d1e3661da","nasal":"73fdf47094c36ad3452a267cefd9329c4374ecb04f0bfe1e8e68cd9d1e3661da"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":7,"english":"And is the mother of the intelligent Rāma, the revered Kausalyā, conversant with virtue and ever practising it, well?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e8477bc54844c24ca45289717ea9ee49fdd1ac4ec26ec913db1132ce04ae85c3","compact":"f78c049b06da3628e85b4932e86b846c3350600b03722abc5fa075f940a4cd11","nasal":"f78c049b06da3628e85b4932e86b846c3350600b03722abc5fa075f940a4cd11"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":8,"english":"Is the virtuous Sumitrā, mother of Lakşmaņa and of the heroic Śatrughna, well?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d2027eeaf5bac971fa696b05c985d161d37a43ce10ceede656b631307cb6498","compact":"1fa052c91f22316d51467eec109f0be84fae6fc334c1453e24ea626204bcbca5","nasal":"1fa052c91f22316d51467eec109f0be84fae6fc334c1453e24ea626204bcbca5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-64-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":64,"verse":9,"english":"And that wrathful one ever intent on her interest and setting immense store by her wisdom, my mother Kaikeyī, is it also well with her?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-70-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2064009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"266